<figure class="diagram bit-order-example">
  <div class="bit-example-equation" aria-label="The service slot value fourteen is binary one one one zero">
    <span>field</span>
    <strong>service slot</strong>
    <span>value</span>
    <code>14 = 1110₂</code>
    <span>starting position</span>
    <code>byte 0, bit 7</code>
  </div>

  <p class="bit-display-note">The bytes use display order <b>bit 7 → bit 0</b>.
  The Sunken cursor starts at bit 0. It moves to bit 7. It then moves to bit 0 of the
  next byte.</p>

  <div class="byte-map" aria-label="Two-byte map showing a service slot split across the byte boundary">
    <div class="byte-row">
      <div class="byte-label"><strong>byte 0</strong><code>11000000₂ = c0₁₆</code></div>
      <div class="byte-bits">
        <div class="bit-piece piece-slot piece-slot-high"
          aria-label="Step 3a: the high bit of service slot 14 is stored in byte 0 bit 7">
          <span class="piece-step">3a</span><b>1</b><small>slot bit 3<br>byte bit 7</small>
        </div>
        <div class="bit-piece piece-flag"
          aria-label="Step 2: the service-present flag is stored in byte 0 bit 6">
          <span class="piece-step">2</span><b>1</b><small>has service<br>byte bit 6</small>
        </div>
        <div class="bit-piece piece-command"
          aria-label="Step 1: command zero occupies byte 0 bits 5 through 0">
          <span class="piece-step">1</span><b>000000</b><small>command 0<br>byte bits 5..0</small>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="byte-wrap" aria-hidden="true"><span>cursor wraps to the next byte</span> ↓</div>

    <div class="byte-row">
      <div class="byte-label"><strong>byte 1</strong><code>ppppp110₂</code></div>
      <div class="byte-bits">
        <div class="bit-piece piece-payload"
          aria-label="Step 4: the payload begins in byte 1 bit 3 and occupies the remaining high bits">
          <span class="piece-step">4</span><b>ppppp</b><small>payload begins<br>byte bits 7..3</small>
        </div>
        <div class="bit-piece piece-slot piece-slot-low"
          aria-label="Step 3b: the remaining low three bits of service slot 14 are stored in byte 1 bits 2 through 0">
          <span class="piece-step">3b</span><b>110</b><small>slot bits 2..0<br>byte bits 2..0</small>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ol class="bit-read-path" aria-label="Logical field-reading order">
    <li><b>1</b><span>command</span></li>
    <li><b>2</b><span>has-service flag</span></li>
    <li class="slot-path"><b>3</b><span>slot <code>1</code> + <code>110</code></span></li>
    <li><b>4</b><span>payload</span></li>
  </ol>

  <div class="bit-order-explainer">
    <p class="bit-order-default"><b>The step numbers show cursor order.</b> The
    diagram uses conventional byte display order. Thus, the bytes match a hex
    dump.</p>
  </div>
</figure>
